    "question_text": "Explain the causes and importance of the monsoon in India.",
    "max_marks": 10,
    "answer_key_text": "The monsoon is caused by differential heating of land and sea. In summer, the land heats up faster than the sea, creating a low-pressure zone over India that draws moist winds from the Indian Ocean. The monsoon brings about 75% of India's annual rainfall and is vital for agriculture.",
